.TH update 1 0.1.2 https://github.com/dbowm91/cargo-cleanme "General Commands Manual"
.SH NAME
update \- Update this cargo\-cleanme to the latest stable published release
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBupdate\fR [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Update this cargo\-cleanme to the latest stable published release.
.PP
The registry is the version authority, the release tag is constructed from that version rather than scraped, and the candidate is replaced only after its `.sha256` evidence is verified and it identifies itself as exactly the target version. A Cargo\-managed installation is refused with the exact manager command, because Cargo owns that file and its bookkeeping.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Resolve the plan and report it without acquiring or replacing bytes
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
